                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Daniel Gaskell was MP for Wakefield 1832-7 and an important philanthropist, especially in matters relating to education and the free church. He was married to 
      <persName key="GAS02">Mary Gaskell</persName> who met <persName key="CLA03">Claire Clairmont</persName> in Pisa. Clairmont introduced her to 
      <persName key="SHE02">Mary Shelley</persName> by letter. The Gaskells were already admirers of Godwin's philosophy and they were keen to meet him.
    </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 14, fol. 110: 18</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"><title>The journals of Mary Shelley, 1814–1844</title>, ed. by Paula R. Feldman and Diana Scott-Kilvert, 2 vols 
  (Oxford and New York: Oxford University Press; Clarendon Press, 1987)</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"><title>The Letters of Charles Dickens</title>, ed. by Madeline House and Graham Storey, 12 vols (Oxford: 
  Clarendon Press, 1965-2002)</bibl>
                </person>
